      "text": "To find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\), we start by examining the given cubic polynomial function \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). We know the graph passes through the points where \\(x = 0, -1, -2\\). \n\nFirst, evaluate the function at \\(x = 0\\):\n\\[\nf(0) = a(0)^3 + b(0)^2 + c(0) + d = d\n\\]\nFrom the graph, we see that \\(f(0) = -8\\), so:\n\\[\nd = -8\n\\]\n\nNext, evaluate the function at \\(x = -1\\):\n\\[\nf(-1) = a(-1)^3 + b(-1)^2 + c(-1) + d = -a + b - c + d\n\\]\nFrom the graph, we see that \\(f(-1) = 0\\), so:\n\\[\n-a + b - c + d = 0\n\\]\nSince \\(d = -8\\), substitute this into the equation:\n\\[\n-a + b - c - 8 = 0 \\implies a - b + c = -8\n\\]\n\nFinally, evaluate the function at \\(x = -2\\):\n\\[\nf(-2) = a(-2)^3 + b(-2)^2 + c(-2) + d = -8a + 4b - 2c + d\n\\]\nFrom the graph, we see that \\(f(-2) = 8\\), so:\n\\[\n-8a + 4b - 2c + d = 8\n\\]\nSince \\(d = -8\\), substitute this into the equation:\n\\[\n-8a + 4b - 2c - 8 = 8 \\implies -8a + 4b - 2c = 16\n\\]\n\nWe now have the system of equations:\n1. \\(a - b + c = -8\\)\n2. \\(-8a + 4b - 2c = 16\\)\n\nTo solve for \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\), we start by rearranging these equations to isolate terms involving \\(8a - 4b + 2c\\):\n3. \\(8a - 4b + 2c = -8a + 16 + c + 8 = -8a + c + 24\\)\n\nThus, substituting these into \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\):\n\\[\n8a - 4b + 2c - d = (8a - 4b + 2c) - d = (-8a + c + 24) - (-8) = -8a + c + 24 + 8 = -8a + c + 32\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve the system to find \\(c\\) and \\(a\\). Starting from \\(a - b + c = -8\\), solve for \\(c\\):\n\\[\nc = -8 - a + b \n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(c\\) into \\(-8a + 4b - 2c = 16\\):\n\\[\n-8a + 4b - 2(-8 - a + b) = 16\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n-8a + 4b + 16 + 2a - 2b = 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-6a + 2b = 0 \\implies b = 3a\n\\]\n\nNow we use \\(b = 3a\\) in \\(c = -8 - a + b\\):\n\\[\nc = -8 - a + 3a = 2a - 8\n\\]\n\nThus, all terms \\(a, b, c, d\\), we substitute \\(b = 3a\\) and \\(c = 2a - 8\\) into the expression:\n\\[\n8a - 4b + 2c = 8a - 4(3a) + 2(2a - 8) = 8a - 12a + 4a - 16\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n8a - 12a + 4a - 16 = 0a - 16 = -16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-16}\n\\]",
