      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) for the cubic function \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we need to determine the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) from the given graph of the function. Let's analyze the graph step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the roots of the function:**\n   From the graph, we can see that the function crosses the x-axis at \\(x = -1\\), \\(x = 1\\), and \\(x = 2\\). This means the roots of the cubic polynomial are given by:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = a(x + 1)(x - 1)(x - 2)\n   \\]\n   Expanding this, we get:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = a(x^3 - x^2 - 2x + 2) = ax^3 - ax^2 - 2ax + 2a\n   \\]\n   By comparing this with the standard form \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we identify:\n   \\[\n   b = -a, \\quad c = -2a, \\quad d = 2a\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\):**\n   Substitute the values of \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) into the expression \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\):\n   \\[\n   8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8a - 4(-a) + 2(-2a) - 2a\n   \\]\n   Simplify the expression:\n   \\[\n   8a + 4a - 4a - 4a - 2a = 8a\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is \\(\\boxed{8a}\\).",
